*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* D-2 witness (GREEN -- THIRD RUNG, s190 seat3): the deferred call is PRESENT but is NOT a  The SECOND claws5 defect, isolated: a DEFERRED CAPTURE
* CAPTURE TARGET -- `*token()` with no leading `.` -- on the same ALT arm inside ARBNO.
* This is what the red/green pair could not separate: their green DELETES the call, so it
* cannot tell 'the deferred call' from 'the capture-target POSITION'.  This rung keeps the
* call and moves it one character, and it is GREEN in BOTH modes -- so the ingredient is the
* POSITION.  A non-capture `*token()` lowers to the ordinary defer road (rt_defer_run_all /
* rt_defer_get_pat_dtp); the capture-target form routes through rt_dcap_pump's by-name dyn
* transfer instead, and that is the road with no mode-4 answer.  Run with SCRIP_SPAN_FRAME=1
* so the s130/s131 leaf-suspension class (the FIRST defect, cured by that arm) is
* out of the way; what remains is m4-only.  rt_dcap_pump reaches the SNOBOL-defined
* target through rt_call_proc_descr's by-name dyn transfer, which in a mode-4 image
* lands on a bogus address (the s156 by-name-dispatch class, D-18's rung).
* Oracle (SPITBOL x64/bin/sbl -b) and SCRIP mode-3 agree; SCRIP mode-4 SIG11s.
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
        DEFINE('token()')  :(token_end)
token   n       =   n + 1
        token   =   .dummy  :(NRETURN)
token_end
        &TRIM   =   0
        n       =   0
        src     =   'ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 ab_A0 '
        p       =   POS(0) ARBNO((SPAN('0123456789') | SPAN('ab') SPAN('_A0') *token()) SPAN(' ')) RPOS(0)
        src     ?   p  :F(error)
        OUTPUT  =   'matched bytes=' SIZE(src) ' n=' n  :(END)
error   OUTPUT  =   'Pattern match failed'
END
